{"from": "passage:lk-10-02", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-37"}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-03", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-16", "note": "Luke: lambs among wolves; Matthew: sheep among wolves."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-09", "note": "Matthew: no gold, silver, copper in money belts; Luke: no purse or wallet."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-10", "note": "Matthew: no bag, two tunics, shoes or staff; Luke: no wallet or sandals. Mark 6:8-9 allows a staff and sandals."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-10", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-14", "note": "Luke adds the public declaration 'the Kingdom of God has come near' to the dust-wiping."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-12", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-10-15", "note": "Matthew: 'the day of judgment'; Luke: 'in that day'."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-13", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-11-21"}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-14", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-11-22"}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-15", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-11-23", "note": "Matthew adds 'for if the mighty works had been done in Sodom...'; Luke omits it."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-11-25", "note": "Luke adds 'rejoiced in the Holy Spirit' and the Son's-knowledge saying of 10:22."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-23", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-13-16", "note": "Luke adds that prophets and kings desired to see these things."}
{"from": "passage:lk-10-27", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-22-37"}
{"from": "claim:lk-10-01-seventy-appointed", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-01-twelve-apostles", "note": "Luke 10:1 sends out seventy (-two) others besides the Twelve; Matthew 10:1 sends the Twelve themselves."}
{"from": "claim:lk-10-19-serpents-scorpions", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-16-serpents", "note": "Luke 10:19 adds scorpions to Matthew 10:16's serpents."}
{"from": "claim:lk-10-35-two-denarii", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-20-02-denarius-a-day", "note": "Luke 10:35: two denarii paid in advance for the wounded man's care; Matthew 20:2: one denarius as the wage for a day's work."}
{"from": "claim:lk-10-38-martha-received", "type": "related_to", "to": "place:bethany", "note": "Luke 10:38 does not name the village; John 11:1 places Martha and Mary in Bethany."}
{"from": "text:numbers-19-11-13", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-10-31-32-corpse-impurity", "note": "Numbers 19:11-13: whoever touches a dead body is unclean seven days - the law the priest's and Levite's avoidance reflects."}
{"from": "site:ascent-of-adummim", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-30-road-robbers", "grade": "B", "note": "The Ascent of Adummim was 'apparently on the road between Jerusalem and Jericho in the Judaean desert' (Joshua 15:7, 18:17) - the route the parable follows."}
{"from": "site:good-samaritan-inn", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-34-inn", "grade": "D", "note": "A 6th-century square inn with rooms, cistern and church for pilgrims on the Jerusalem-Jericho road: inns existed on the route, but five centuries after the parable, and the identification with the parable's inn is tradition, not evidence."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-2-bethboron", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-30-road-robbers", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus: robbers attacked a servant of Caesar 'at the public road at Beth-boron' (c. 48 CE) - robbers seizing a traveler on a Judean public road; the Beth-horon road is not the Jericho road."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-4-jericho-road", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-30-road-robbers", "grade": "B", "note": "Josephus on Jericho: 'The country, as far as Jerusalem, is desert and stony' - the same Jerusalem-Jericho route described by a contemporary; it attests the setting, not the robbery."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-oholot-2-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-31-32-corpse-impurity", "grade": "B", "note": "Oholot 2:1 lists what 'defile by overshadowing: a corpse...' - the tractate of corpse impurity; redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe 30 CE practice exactly. Regraded C to B per the architect's Mishnah ruling (2026-11-15): the Mishnah names the same practice the claim states."}
{"from": "observation:deathstalker-range", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-19-serpents-scorpions", "grade": "C", "note": "The deathstalker is 'found in desert and scrubland habitats ranging from North Africa through to the Middle East' - a highly venomous scorpion of the wider region; the source names no first-century Judea, and the range is present-day."}
{"from": "artifact:denarius", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-10-35-two-denarii", "grade": "C", "note": "The denarius was the standard Roman silver coin used for a day's wage, so 'two denarii' named a real, countable sum (reused from Matt 20:2). Regraded B to C by architect review: the denarius is context (C) everywhere in the graph."}
{"from": "site:ascent-of-adummim", "type": "related_to", "to": "place:jerusalem", "note": "The ascent is the beginning of the road up from Jericho to Jerusalem."}
